e UI thread. ---> System.InvalidCastException...`\n- **Screenshot:** Uploaded an image showing the History screen with a red warning triangle reading \"خطأ في جلب السجل\" (Error fetching history).\n\n### API Keys & Credentials\n- **MSEMAX API Key**: `[REDACTED_CREDENTIAL]` (Server at `D:\\AI_Engineer\\MSEMAX\\`)\n- **Unstructured.io API Key**: stored in project `.env` file at `d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\.env`\n\n---\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n\n- **Fixed Duplicate Processes & History (Completed):** Added logic in `start_process` to check the DB for identical inputs with a 'completed' status to skip redundant processing. Added `mark_stuck_processes_as_failed()` to `database.py` running on app boot so any crashed/aborted processes don't remain \"قيد التشغيل\" (Processing) forever.\n- **Fixed `OPEN_DIALOG` Deprecation Warning (Completed):** Updated `backend.py` to use `getattr(webview, 'FileDialog', webview).OPEN` so the user no longer sees the misleading \"future version\" warning in the terminal.\n- **Fixed Process Submission Glitch & Added Progress Bar (Completed):** UI no longer jumps to \"0 0 0\" results. It now increments `window.activeProcesses`, stays on the submission page, and updates a visual progress bar (10% -> 30% -> 60% -> 90%) using `process_update` events before automatically navigating upon receiving `process_complete`.\n- **Fixed Application Scroll/Responsiveness (Completed):** Updated CSS `.main-content` flex properties and removed `min-height: 100vh` to eliminate the ugly double scrollbar.\n- **Fixed Exit Deadlock & Added Warning (Completed):** Hooked into `exitApp()` to check `window.activeProcesses > 0` and display a confirmation warning. Used `os._exit(0)` for instant, freeze-free shutdowns.\n- **Fixed Drag & Drop Deadlock (Completed):** Bypassed Edge WebView2 security restrictions on local file paths by using HTML5 `FileReader` (Base64) to transfer dropped files directly to Python memory and saving them to `%TEMP%`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n\n### Architecture & Fixes\n- **COM / UI Thread Bug (NEW):** Pywebview on Windows (using Edge Chromium/WebView2) is highly sensitive to thread access. The JS calling `window.pywebview.api.delete_process()` followed rapidly by `window.pywebview.api.get_history()` appears to be causing a COM exception: `CoreWebView2Controller members can only be accessed from the UI thread`. This breaks the IPC bridge, returning `undefined` or throwing in JS, causing the `catch` block in `loadHistory()` to display \"خطأ في جلب السجل\".\n- **Database Schema:** `processes` table uses `id`, `created_at`, `status`, `shortage_files`, `warehouse_files`. Previously, JS was incorrectly trying to read `item.processId` and `item.timestamp`. This has been fixed in `index.html`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\backend.py`**\n  - *Changes*: Updated `select_files` to use `FileDialog.OPEN` (silencing deprecation warning). Added a call to `self.db.mark_stuck_processes_as_failed()` in `__init__`. Fixed result DB updates in `_process_worker` to properly map `results.get(\"summary\")` and emit correct JS events.\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\database.py`**\n  - *Changes*: Added `mark_stuck_processes_as_failed(self)` method to bulk-update `status = 'processing'` to `error`.\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\templates\\index.html`**\n  - *Changes*: Updated `process_update` listener to target `#progress-text` and an animated `#progress-bar-fill`. Fixed `loadHistory` JS keys mapping (`created_at`, `id`). Fixed `viewProcess` JS to properly map `total_shortages` into the expected `stats` object format. Fixed scrolling layout CSS. Added an exit warning block in `exitApp`. Added `resetNewProcessForm()` call when navigating back to `screen-new`.\n\n### Viewed Files\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\app.py`**\n  - *Context*: Verified window creation. The app initializes without `maximized=True` but the user still saw a `Maximized.Maximized: maximum recursion depth exceeded` exception in the terminal. This is a known pywebview quirk on Windows and was explained to the user.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n**Current Status:** I just resolved all previously outstanding UI/UX complaints, database stuck states, and terminal deprecation warnings. However, the user immediately hit a new issue: trying to delete an item from the history screen threw a massive COM WebView2 exception in the terminal and displayed \"خطأ في جلب السجل\" (Error fetching history) on the UI.\n\n**Next Steps for the Next Agent:**\n1. **Investigate the History Fetch/Delete COM Exception:**\n   - Look at `d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\backend.py` (`delete_process` and `get_history`).\n   - The crash indicates `CoreWebView2Controller members can only be accessed from the UI thread`. This often happens if the python code inside the API class attempts to interact with the window incorrectly, OR it might just be a `pywebview` version bug triggered by rapid consecutive calls (`delete_process` awaiting, then `get_history` awaiting).\n   - Try wrapping the API calls or isolating them. Ensure no `evaluate_js` is being triggered simultaneously that clashes with the data return. \n   - Check if `sqlite3` cross-thread issues are somehow bubbling up and causing the IPC to fail. Add extensive try/except blocks inside `get_history` and `delete_process` to return clean JSON error messages instead of letting exceptions bubble to the WebView2 COM layer.\n\nYou have the 15 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/desktop-builder/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:17:02Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/pharmacy-builder/agent.md\nLast