{"step_index":629,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T00:06:22Z","thinking":"**Locating Missing Function**\n\nOkay, so I got ahead of myself. I jumped the gun and assumed I'd written a `deleteProcess` function in the JavaScript. Turns out, I didn't. I'm seeing it referenced on line 1410 with the `onclick` attribute, but the function's definition is nowhere to be found. The search continues...\n\n\n**Analyzing the Error Source**\n\nOkay, so I got ahead of myself. I jumped the gun and assumed I'd written a `deleteProcess` function in the JavaScript. Turns out, I didn't. I'm seeing it referenced on line 1410 with the `onclick` attribute, but the function's definition is nowhere to be found. The search continues...\n\nI realized I missed defining `deleteProcess` in `index.html`. That explains the `ReferenceError`. However, the user also saw \"خطأ في جلب السجل\" and that's concerning. That's only displayed if `loadHistory()` fails within its `catch` block. I need to understand why `loadHistory()` would fail, and I'm suspecting data corruption in the `shortage_files` JSON. The user's description hints at other issues: two processes running, deleting something in-use.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Inspect DB","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"import sqlite3, json, sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nDATA_DIR = Path('d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/data')\nDB_PATH = DATA_DIR / 'history.db'\n\nif not DB_PATH.exists():\n    print(\"DB does not exist.\")\n    sys.exit(0)\n\nconn = sqlite3.connect(DB_PATH)\nconn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\nc = conn.cursor()\nc.execute('SELECT * FROM processes')\nrows = [dict(row) for row in c.fetchall()]\n\nfor i, row in enumerate(rows):\n    print(f\"Row {i}:\")\n    for k, v in row.items():\n        print(f\"  {k}: {repr(v)}\")\n","Description":"Inspect history.db","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\kakak\\.gemini\\ant