{"step_index":647,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T00:11:26Z","thinking":"**Considering Confirmation Options**\n\nI'm now exploring alternatives to the `confirm()` function. A custom HTML modal seems like a viable solution, or maybe just bypassing the confirmation step entirely, depending on the situation. I'll need to assess the project's existing dependencies to see if `sweetalert2` is already integrated; if not, a simple HTML modal might suffice.\n\n\n**Analyzing Threading Issues**\n\nI've pinpointed the root cause! The UI thread errors arise because the Python-JS bridge in `pywebview` attempts WebView2 access from a background thread. This happens when `loadHistory` runs after `deleteProcess`. Since deleting calls `loadHistory` directly, the UI thread gets messed up and `get_history` fails, which throws a COM exception. A simple fix would be to make `deleteProcess` await the UI Thread.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\kakak\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\.system_generated\\tasks\\task-646.log","toolAction":"Read log","toolSummary":"Read log"}}]}
